ck towns in the Midwest by a pious mother and a reckless, alcoholic, largely absent father. Severely near-sighted, the boy lives in his own world, a world of the popular books of the day, and finds his first brush with popularity, even fame, as a young lifeguard. Thanks to his first great love, he imagines a way out, and makes the extraordinary leap to go to college, a modest school by national standards, but an audacious presumption in the context of his family's station. From there, the path is only very dimly lit, but it leads him, thanks to his great charm and greater luck, to a solid career as a radio sportscaster, and then, astonishingly, fatefully, to Hollywood. And the rest, as they say, is history.","pageCount":863,"publicationYear":2018,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Governors","sourceId":"source-open-library-reagan-an-american-journey-bob-spitz"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Presidents","sourceId":"source-open-library-reagan-an-american-journey-bob-spitz"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-reagan-an-american-journey-bob-spitz"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Motion picture actors and actresses","sourceId":"source-open-library-reagan-an-american-journey-bob-spitz"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Reagan, ronald, 1911-2004","sourceId":"source-open-library-reagan-an-american-journey-bob-spitz"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Presidents, united states","sourceId":"source-open-library-reagan-an-american-journey-bob-spitz"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Governors, united states","sourceId":"source-open-library-reagan-an-american-journey-bob-spitz"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Motion picture actors and actresses, united st